    description: "FOUND 2026-09-24 while measuring WI-narij (surveys at dev 944735a08f; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/narij_09242026/).\n\nTHE DEFECT: the scala analyzer resolves a call by the callee's SIMPLE NAME across the whole repository and ignores the calling file's explicit import. The edge is origin `scala`, confidence 0.8 (0.85 for one).\n- spark: core/src/main/scala/org/apache/spark/TestUtils.scala (package org.apache.spark) has `import scala.sys.process.Process`. Its `Process(cmdSeq :+ ...).!` resolves to the `case class Process` nested in sql/core/src/test/.../ForeachWriterSuite.scala, in another package. That is 12 edges of this shape on spark.\n- scala3: bin/test/TestScripts.scala has `import scala.sys.process.{Process, ProcessLogger}`. Its `Process(script) ! ...` resolves to `object Process` in the sbt build's project/Process.scala. That is 10 edges.\n\nCONSEQUENCES:\n1. A FALSE call edge to the wrong callee, which feeds the call graph, slices and dead-code.\n2. The real launch disappears. A resolved edge never reaches the io catalogue, so these subprocess launches classify as nothing even after WI-narij.\n`_is_project_type` (scala.py) is name-based in the same way. WI-kilap's static_owner_module relies on it to refuse the import path for a project type.\n\nASKED:\n- An explicit import in the calling file must outrank a same-named project symbol from another package, unless the import itself names a project path.\n- Fix in the producer.\n- Measure the resolved-edge diff on the scala cohort, as a set not a count. Detekt's imported project type (WI-kilap's regression test) must keep resolving.\n- Check kotlin for the same shape. Not checked."  # 3f7c
